{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals","id":849962,"title":"If I were writing Sidereals...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-19T19:12:59-07:00","id":849962,"title":"If I were writing Sidereals...","content":"If I were writing Sidereals...<br /> <br /> GOALS:<br /> * Fold Astrology into their Charms; leave larger workings as a specialization of the Sorcerous Project system.<br /> * Emphasize the planning and preparation nature of Sidereals- their best effects require they don astrological masks and stay within an archtype, or generate omens and prophecies that can forewarn enemies.<br /> * Make being Outside of Fate more of a lateral move than straight benefit.<br /> * Keep as many of the 1e Ability &lt;--&gt; Constellation associations as possible.<br /> * Solve the 'Every Sidereal has to favor Martial Arts' problem.<br /> <br /> NOT GOALS:<br /> * Binding to the same Charm Trees exactly as in 1e or 2e. Although I'm striving for a 1e feel, that's as a guide, not a straightjacket.<br /> * Maintaining Prayer Strip capstones. Prayer Strip charms are powerful and useful- but they don't suit as the capstone to every ability.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Some general notes regarding the Sidereal Exalted:<br /> <br /> **ARCANE FATE**<br /> Due to the shattering of the Mask, the Sidereals slip from the memory of the world.<br /> At the end of any scene, all mortals who do not have at least a trivial intimacy towards the Sidereal begin to forget about them- by the end of the next scene, they retain only the haziest of memories.<br /> At the end of each story, all characters who have an Intimacy, positive or negative, towards either a Sidereal in particular or towards Sidereals as a whole are subject to a 10 dice social influence action to weaken the Intimacy, supported by a Major Intimacy. This influence occurs once per appropriate Intimacy.<br /> A character who has their last Intimacy towards a Sidereal erased by this will forget the Sidereal entirely; likewise towards collective Intimacies.<br /> <br /> A character who holds no intimacies towards Sidereals, either singularly or collectively, is at a significant disadvantage in learning anything about them. Knowledge of the Sidereal Exalted is naturally hard to come by, and the world seeks to erase their presence.<br /> Such a character incurs a -3 situational penalty on any attempt to learn or reveal information about the Sidereal Exalted.<br /> <br /> **RESPLENDENT DESTINIES**<br /> When a Sidereal needs to interact with the world for an extended period, they will most often do so by weaving themselves into the story as an appropriate character- an act they call donning a Resplendent Destiny.<br /> Each Ability has a Charm, 'Resplendent Destiny of (Constellation)'<br /> With each purchase, the Sidereal crafts a new persona, much as the Solar Charm 'Heart-Eclipsing Shroud', although the specifics of what the new persona's design vary by constellation.<br /> These personas are not touched by Arcane Fate; mortals will remember interactions with them normally, and intimacies formed to them will not fade under the vagaries of Arcane Fate. This is true even when the Sidereal is not wearing the Destiny.<br /> <br /> Resplendent Destinies are fragile; they immediately end if the Sidereal grossly violates their role or if their anima flares to bonfire level. They can also always be ended as a simple act of will, requiring a Simple action and 1 Willpower.<br /> <br /> Donning a Resplendent Destiny can be done for free over the course of five hours spent wearing the trappings of the Constellation and without violating the associations, or as a Simple action for 10m.<br /> Resplendent Destinies can provide minor cosmetic changes to a character's appearance, but only to the extent of a mortal disguise. They do not overtly change a character's clothing or possessions- and a character who is dressed too far out of character for a given Destiny may have it shatter as soon as it's donned.<br /> <br /> **DESIGNS OF DESTINY**<br /> Several Sidereal Charms allow them to describe, within some limitations, some set of circumstances under which an individual or activity is especially propitious or baneful. Such Charms have the keyword 'Design'.<br /> Once a Design is undertaken, until either the Sidereal releases the committed motes or the Design is fulfilled, Creation will begin to bring forth omens and prophecies, letting those with the appropriate Lores or thaumaturgical gifts insight into the Designs.<br /> Many Sidereals, given the chance, will set up multiple favorable designs upon themselves and their allies, and then endeavor to ensure that they are fulfilled just when needed.<br /> Unless otherwise noted, recognizing and correctly interpreting the omens and portents that herald a Design is an Intelligence + Lore action, with a difficulty of (8 - Charm's Essence). If you have an intimacy towards the Sidereal who enacted the Design, you gain a +3 situational bonus. This does not tell you exactly what the Design's effect is, but gives you an educated guess and a heads up.<br /> <br /> **OUTSIDE OF FATE**<br /> Many of the Sidereal's most powerful charms relate to altering someone's role within the weave of the world upon the Loom of Fate.<br /> These powers also work similarly upon those beings who's story is told in the constellations of the Underworld, the broken stars of Malfaes, or the ever-changing story of the Wyld- although sometimes less effaciously.<br /> <br /> Especially potent individuals, however, have no part in any weave- they stand apart, and no destiny helps or hinders them. Such beings are said to be outside of Fate.<br /> Such beings are not subject to Arcane Fate, and always only perceive a Sidereal as themselves, even when they have donned a Resplendent Destiny.<br /> Likewise, they are secure in their mind, body, destiny and location- they ignore effects which would alter their TNs, cost or grant Willpower, add or remove Intimacies, or change their location.<br /> To their detriment, however, this can leave them out of step with everything else that is. When someone Outside of Fate directly acts against the designs of destiny, they suffer a -3 situational penalty to all actions for the remainder of the scene- having fallen out of step with the world, they find themselves improvising, like an actor that has forgotten their lines.<br /> Additionally, when such a violation occurs within Creation, the Bureau of Destiny is often notified. If such a violation occurs against a specific Sidereal's designs, then that Sidereal is alerted, regardless of the location.<br /> Individuals inside Fate can also act against the designs of fate, and do so without risk to the overall weave. Instead, they will have to contend with the powers of the agents of destiny directly.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb, only the following entities or individuals of similar power and scope are outside of Fate:<br /> * The Incarna<br /> * The Demon Princes and their Third Circle Souls<br /> * The Neverborn and the Deathlords<br /> * Fair Folk of the Ishvara<br /> * Rakan Thulio<br /> <br /> Certain Charms, powers, spells or sorcerous working can also remove an individual from Fate, either temporarily or permanently. Likewise, some of these individuals can be drawn into the weave of Fate again, although usually for only a limited time.<br /> <br /> **MASTERS OF THE MARTIAL ARTS**<br /> All Sidereals gain the Martial Arts merit for free, and always purchase dots of the Martial Arts abilities and charms as favored even if they do not favor Brawl.<br /> <br /> **FAVORED AND FATED ABILITIES**<br /> Sidereals have 9 Favored Abilities; at least 3 of them must be from Caste Abilities.<br /> Additionally, one of their Favored Caste Abilities is their Fated Ability.<br /> Much as the Solar Exalted are noted to excel with a particular supernal ability, each of the Sidereals has an ability with which they are Fated to master.<br /> Sidereals gain the Resplendent Destiny of their Fated Ability for free. When they don this Resplendent Destiny, they may treat their Essence and Ability as 5 for all Charms of the Fated Ability.<br /> They may also treat their Essence and Ability rating as 5 for the purposes of learning the Charms of their Fated Ability- but they may only use those Charms for which they do not naturally qualify when they don the Resplendent Destiny.<br /> <br /> **ANIMA EFFECTS**<br /> (I am honestly drawing a blank on most of these)<br /> <br /> **CASTE ABILITIES AND CONSTELLATIONS**<br /> The House of Journeys<br /> Resistance (The Mast), Ride (The Messenger), Sail (The Captain), Survival (The Ship's Wheel), Thrown (The Gull)<br /> <br /> The House of Serenity<br /> Craft (The Peacock), Dodge (The Ewer), Linguistics (The Pillar), Performance (The Musician), Socialize (The Lovers)<br /> <br /> The House of Battles<br /> Archery (The Quiver), Brawl (The Gauntlet), Melee (The Spear), Presence (The Shield), War (The Banner)<br /> <br /> The House of Secrets<br /> Investigation (The Key), Larceny (The Guardians), Lore (The Treasure Trove), Occult (The Sorcerer), Stealth (The Mask)<br /> <br /> The House of Endings<br /> Athletics (The Rising Smoke), Awareness (The Crow), Bureaucracy (The Haywain), Integrity (The Sword), Medicine (The Corpse)<br /> <br /> Changes from first edition:<br /> Endurance and Resistance collapse together under the Mast<br /> War introduced, under the Banner. Presence moved to the Shield.<br /> Integrity replaces Martial Arts under the Sword.<br /> <br /> Changelog<br /> * Added difficulty for understanding omens caused by Designs.<br /> * Changed Master of the Martial Arts to give the merit free and explicitly make purchasing dots cost favored as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 03-21-2016, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T19:14:51-07:00","id":849964,"title":"","content":"Resistance: THE MAST<br /> Trappings: The Mast is drably dressed and unspeaking. They are strong and honest but ignorant.<br /> Associations: Stoicism, tools, architecture, manual labor, silence, ignorance, phallus<br /> <br /> The Scripture of the Eternal Maiden<br /> Once, there was a maiden...<br /> ... made from a lump of iron, shaped by wind, sea and fire<br /> Fearing how wood might shape her, she ran, and did not look back<br /> One day she forgot what she ran from<br /> So, she pulled out her heart to ask it.<br /> &quot;Why don't you look back and see?&quot; it said.<br /> So, she sighed and threw her heart away.<br /> &quot;I have no use for beginnings&quot; said she.<br /> <br /> -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-<br /> <br /> Resplendent Destiny of the Mast<br /> Cost: - (10m); Mins: Resistance 1, Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> The Sidereal creates a new persona, a character of the Mast. The intimacies selected must be appropriate for an archtype of the Mast, relating to the appropriate associations.<br /> For example, the Resplendent Destiny may have a tie of admiration towards Ragara Yukio, a noted architect and geomancer; or perhaps a principle of disdain towards scholars and other individuals of book learning.<br /> <br /> While wearing this Resplendent Destiny, you must redistribute any dots you have in Linguistics, Investigation, Socialize, Lore or Bureaucracy amongst your other abilities.<br /> You may not have more than 1 dot in any of those Abilities while in this Destiny.<br /> You may raise Resistance to 6 while under the Resplendent Destiny of the Mast. Additionally, in any populated area, they can find a menial job that will ensure they are fed, clothed and sheltered from the elements.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Ox-Body Technique<br /> Cost: -; Mins: Resistance 1, Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Stackable<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> As per the Solar Charm 'Ox-Body Technique', except:<br /> <br /> Stamina 1-2: An additional -1 health level<br /> Stamina 3-4: An additional -0 health level<br /> Stamina 5+: An additional -0 and -2 health levels<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Strength of the Mast<br /> Cost: 3m / dot; Mins: Resistance 3, Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Resplendent Destiny of the Mast<br /> <br /> The Mast is always strong enough to do whatever job they have. When performing a feat of strength, they may increase their Strength up to the strongest person in the area, plus their Essence. This increase only enables their ability to perform the feat- it does not add to their dicepool for succeeding.<br /> When wearing the Destiny of the Mast, Strength of the Mast costs 2m per dot.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Someone Else's Destiny<br /> Cost: (Intervals) m, 1wp; Mins: Resistance 4, Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> Poison and toxins cannot slow the Chosen of Journeys- mostly because they were always destined for another. When exposed to a toxin, you may activate Someone Else's Destiny; it costs one Willpower and a number of motes equal to the total duration of the effect.<br /> The poison ceases to exist, save as a memo attached to the Sidereal's destiny. They may unleash it as a Gambit (difficulty 3) against a target within the scene, or allow it to disperse without effect.<br /> Someone Else's Destiny may not be used while in Initative Crash.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Unswerving Juggernaut Principle<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Resistance 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Design<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charm: None<br /> <br /> The Sidereal writes their intention and weaves their arrival into the pattern of destiny, as well as when they will arrive. Omens and signs begin to appear at the destination, heralding the arrival of the Chosen.<br /> The destination must be, as far as the Sidereal knows, reachable through pure physical movement (walking, climbing or sailing) within the given timeframe.<br /> As long as they do nothing but travel towards their destination, re-roll 1s on any contested roll which could prevent you from arriving.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Optimistic Security Practice<br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Resistance 2, Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Someone Else's Destiny<br /> <br /> Some people do not know how to stay down; some people are too stupid and stubborn to die. Such ignorance can be awe-inspiring.<br /> When activated against a withering attack, Optimistic Security Practice increases your bashing, lethal and aggravated soak by Essence + Resistance. If you are wearing armor, it only increases your soak by Essence.<br /> When activated against a decisive attack, Optimistic Security Practice provides a number of -0 health levels equal to your Essence. (As per Iron Skin Concentration)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Water and Fire Designs<br /> Cost: 3m, 1wp, 1lhl; Mins: Resistance 5, Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Design<br /> Duration: Until Calibration<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> A sacrifice of blood, either given to a bonfire or a large body of water, secures you from being harmed by the designated element for the remainder of the year.<br /> If the design is enacted upon fire, you suffer no damage or impairment from natural flames, although may still be burned by magical fire- such as a bolt from a Dragonblooded, or a sorcerous attack.<br /> If the design is enacted upon water, you cannot drown, and may move freely in water.<br /> Water and Fire Designs cannot be used during Calibration, and cannot be in effect for both fire and water at the same time.<br /> After being enacted, until it is released, omens will surround you, informing those who look into your destiny of the bargain you have struck.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3, Water and Fire Designs can be purchased a second time. If they do, then by touching an appropriately aspected spirit (which may require a Brawl or Martial Arts gambit, difficulty 1), you may attempt to bind them into protecting a place until Calibration.<br /> Make a Charisma + Resistance roll, against a difficulty of the spirit's Resolve. If successful, the spirit gains an unbreakable Defining Principle towards the task you describe until Calibration.<br /> The omens shift to indicate this protection over the location, rather than the Sidereal's person.<br /> Doing so ends the protection provided by Water and Fire Designs. Re-enacting the protection renders the principle no longer unbreakable and reduces it to a Major Principle.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Shield of Destiny<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Resistance 5, Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Counterattack, Decisive-only, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> Those who try to tear down the Mast often find the task is beyond their ken or expectation- even when they succeed, the fall is likely to ruin them as well.<br /> When subject to a decisive attack, you may use Shield of Destiny. Roll Stamina + Resistance; each success reduces the initiative pool of the attacker by 1. If your successes are greater than their initiative, then you crash them.<br /> After their attack is resolved, you may make a decisive counterattack.<br /> When wearing the Destiny of the Mast, double 8s on both the Stamina + Resistance roll and the counterattack.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Heartless Maiden Trance<br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp; Mins: Resistance 5, Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Unswerving Juggernaut Principle<br /> <br /> You swallow your heart and still your breath. While active, you ignore the mundane needs of your body for food, water and rest, as well as any penalties you suffer from injury or exposure. If you are exposed to an illness or poison, it is automatically held in abeyance.<br /> You cannot be knocked unconcious; instead, you will only be killed if you take a number of levels of damage equal to your Stamina.<br /> However, you also cease to respire motes; until Heartless Maiden Trance is released, you do not gain motes outside of combat, and only gain 3 motes per round instead of 5 during combat.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Storm's Eye Stance<br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp; Mins: Resistance 5, Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Design<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Strength of the Mast, Optimistic Security Practice, Water and Fire Designs, Shield of Destiny, Heartless Maiden Trance<br /> <br /> You inscribe a time and place upon a prayer strip inscribed with The Scripture of the Eternal Maiden, and then cast it either into fire or water, whereupon it vanishes in a golden light.<br /> It appears again in the hands of whomever you wish. Make a Charisma + Resistance roll against their Resolve to persuade them to seek you out at the named place and time, as if backed by a Major intimacy.<br /> The time and place must be somewhere you can reach within one lunar month, and must be at least one week from the time you use Storm's Eye Stance. The time may be ambigious- for example, 'When the courtyard shines bright as noon' could be satisfied at noon, or at midnight- if you have taken pains to ensure that enough bonfires have been lit to make it as bright as noon.<br /> At the time and place you describe, you may fulfil this design, placing yourself at the center of the storm.<br /> Until the end of the scene, you ignore onslaught penalties. When enemies attack you with withering attacks, you steal 1 point of initiative for each 1 or 2 they roll, and reduce all withering damage to minimum. Add your Resistance in bonus dice to any roll made to rush or disengage.<br /> If you wear the Destiny of the Mast from the time you begin the design until it is fulfilled, you also re-roll 7s, 8s, 9s and 10s on any actions you take for the scene.<br /> <br /> CHANGELOG:<br /> * Slightly bumped Ox-Body Technique","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 03-21-2016, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T10:13:58-07:00","id":850173,"title":"","content":"Positively, keeps it nice and simple by rolling together astro and charms, looking functional and engaging and await to see how Celestial Astrology, the kind that affects the destinies of others, is worked in through Sorcerous Workings (and Charms).<br /> <br /> Critically:<br /> <br /> - Omens seem like an interesting idea; as who doesn't want to be the mover of fates whose arrival is heralded by signs and portents, and it would shut down some of the &quot;Bah. Sidereals everybody just gettin' Si-dereals leaping on up at them out damn teacups up in hiyah!&quot; grumbles.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Sidereal are supposed to be secret and act secretly. I feel also omens might be more practical with guidance on how they actually affect things, like difficulties on Lore and Occult, if used against quantified NPCs etc. An omen an average DB can read is different from one a No Moon with specialist training at understanding fate can read, is different from one an experienced Sidereal only can read. e.g. If a character could already use their Lore to see your coming, how much easier (if at all) do omens (like those with Unswerving Juggernaut Principle) make it? I'm a bit leery of it being &quot;as much as your group reckons&quot;, opposed to having at least some defined baseline that Sidereal players can try to game to their advantage / disadvantage. Although perhaps that's the most practical solution (avoiding heavy blocks of text etc.).<br /> <br /> - I'm kind of into a Sidereal design that allows spontaneity if you're able to, and encourages planning if not. More than a &quot;this must be done in advance&quot; design. Just as a general point, in favour against trying to design *too* much obligate planning steps into Sidereal magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T11:20:00-07:00","id":850201,"title":"","content":"I love the Arcane Fate part and it's interaction with Intimacies. I have a rough draft of my thoughts on the Loom of Fate and I have a section on how it ties in to Intimacies. I also have immunity to Arcane Fate is based on access to the Loom of Fate. For example, gods of the Bureau of Destiny, Celestial Lions, Auditors, and Sidereal Half Castes that work for the Bureau have access to the Loom of Fate and thus are immune to Arcane Fate. Creatures outside of Fate are also immune until they gain a thread on the Loom.<br /> <br /> Yes to folding Astrology Resplendency powers into charms! I rarely see Resplendency powers used in games.<br /> <br /> About planning and Sidereals. I also prefer more Spontaneity in Sidereal design. Yes, planning and foresight does play into the Sidereal themes, but sometimes we need to set that aside for what makes an interesting play experience. I would prefer Sidereals to have more options for when things don't go according to play beyond Avoidance Kata.<br /> <br /> Also, the less Destiny Taxes the better. Let's make Sidereal paperwork a flavor joke or stunt fodder instead of having a sidereal make six rolls for one Astrology effect. (I should probably note, I have played a lot of Fate in my day, so I will always side on &quot;the Less Rules the Better&quot; and &quot;Only Roll if Failure is Interesting&quot;)<br /> <br /> I don't see a problem with all Sidereals favoring Martial Arts. Martial Arts, especially Sidereal Martial Arts, encompass more than just smacking people with your fist (which is why I disagree with needing a point of brawl for MA, but that is another argument). I hope in 3rd Edition, Sidereals get that merit for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-20-2016, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T11:25:23-07:00","id":850204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850201#post850201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope in 3rd Edition, Sidereals get that merit for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Ability favoured whether or not they favour Brawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T11:52:56-07:00","id":850212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850173#post850173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Omens seem like an interesting idea; as who doesn't want to be the mover of fates whose arrival is heralded by signs and portents, and it would shut down some of the &quot;Bah. Sidereals everybody just gettin' Si-dereals leaping on up at them out damn teacups up in hiyah!&quot; grumbles.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Sidereal are supposed to be secret and act secretly. I feel also omens might be more practical with guidance on how they actually affect things, like difficulties on Lore and Occult, if used against quantified NPCs etc. An omen an average DB can read is different from one a No Moon with specialist training at understanding fate can read, is different from one an experienced Sidereal only can read. e.g. If a character could already use their Lore to see your coming, how much easier (if at all) do omens (like those with Unswerving Juggernaut Principle) make it? I'm a bit leery of it being &quot;as much as your group reckons&quot;, opposed to having at least some defined baseline that Sidereal players can try to game to their advantage / disadvantage. Although perhaps that's the most practical solution (avoiding heavy blocks of text etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree. Designs and Omens are one of those things that I can totally see how I want to use them as an ST with Sidereal NPCs- but am still feeling out the rules for using them as a player.<br /> My bowel cognition is that the difficulty should be around 7 - (Essence); with more potent charms generating more and more obvious portents. Alternatively, it could be defined in each Charm distinctly but man, that's a lot of word count for something of marginal value.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850173#post850173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- I'm kind of into a Sidereal design that allows spontaneity if you're able to, and encourages planning if not. More than a &quot;this must be done in advance&quot; design. Just as a general point, in favour against trying to design *too* much obligate planning steps into Sidereal magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>My aim is around 1/4 of the Charms should be Designs or otherwise require notable planning, and 1/4 should benefit from being in the appropriate Destiny- useful with an upside. The rest should be as utilitious as Solar Charms","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T12:44:58-07:00","id":850221,"title":"","content":"At a glance...<br /> <br /> The Maidens and Rakan Thulio really shouldn't be outside Fate. They're as inside as anyone can possibly be. Dunno about the other Incarnae, either.<br /> <br /> New Ox-Body looks really weak.<br /> <br /> Martial Artist should probably be completely free for Sids.<br /> <br /> I don't think that take on Resplendent Destinies is a good idea. Letting Sidereals muck with ability dots like that basically means that they all have 5 (or occasionally 6) dots in every ability as long as they have motes to spend or time to prepare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T15:46:42-07:00","id":850286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850212#post850212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely agree. Designs and Omens are one of those things that I can totally see how I want to use them as an ST with Sidereal NPCs- but am still feeling out the rules for using them as a player.<br /> <br /> My bowel cognition is that the difficulty should be around 7 - (Essence); with more potent charms generating more and more obvious portents. Alternatively, it could be defined in each Charm distinctly but man, that's a lot of word count for something of marginal value.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense and is concise. Although it depends on what you want to do with the omens for higher Essence Charms. Are they the key to avoiding and preventing such powerful and devilishly subtle magic that only a true master of Lore could see them coming? As a challenge to high Lore players faced with a Sidereal opponent (only they can see the signs) or PC Sidereals faced with a the same high Lore opponent. In which case they should have pretty high difficulty. Or more the significant drawback and balance to some seriously high power Charms, where it makes sense that the Charm's power is such that even a person of quite low learning can feel it in the air, and in the water, when it is coming for them? This is as a drawback for Sidereal players to consider and to have to use their subterfuge and cunning if they want to conceal the omen. In which case decreasing difficulty with higher essence works well. I feel like the latter for sure is more your goal, but wanted to sound that one out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850221#post850221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Maidens and Rakan Thulio really shouldn't be outside Fate. They're as inside as anyone can possibly be. Dunno about the other Incarnae, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think for the Maidens (less sure about Rakan) and the Incarna, it's more &quot;What the Christ are you talking about, Sidereal? *You* don't get to say what's fated. *I'm* the one that says what's fated&quot; more than them actually being *outside* of Fate, if a Sidereal were to use a Charm on them to dictate their destiny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850221#post850221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that take on Resplendent Destinies is a good idea. Letting Sidereals muck with ability dots like that basically means that they all have 5 (or occasionally 6) dots in every ability as long as they have motes to spend or time to prepare.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the issue with this. At the same time, simply losing access to the dots is kind of less than satisfactory. Spitballing, maybe another way to do it might be allow the Sidereal to &quot;shuck&quot; role inappropriate ratings off onto a loyal familar spirit, or another Sidereal ally, or a suitable attuned artefact, and that destiny simply allows such limited reallocations. More like you're stashing your skills somewhere still fairly accessible than rechanneling them into different Abilities. Some form where the mighty warrior who adopts the Resplendent Destiny of a feeble weakling trades away her Melee for a powerful guardian spirit familiar or a wise savant who loses their Lore gains an trustworthy advisor. Fate arranges that her Abilities are rechanneled in a way that does not lessen her capabilities, or her circle's, within that area. Maybe that would have even more issues, though, and it simply makes more sense to allow dot reallocation with &quot;no-shenanigans&quot; and that dot reallocation wouldn't actually be much of an issue in reality (if continuing with that form of Resplendent Destiny)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T17:13:15-07:00","id":850327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850221#post850221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At a glance...<br /> <br /> The Maidens and Rakan Thulio really shouldn't be outside Fate. They're as inside as anyone can possibly be. Dunno about the other Incarnae, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rakan Thulio sure the hell is outside of Fate. Saturn made her mark against him, and he went 'Fuck that shit', then tore his thread from the Loom with blasphemous power. Dude is out of fate as fuck.<br /> <br /> The Maidens and the Incarna- it's more a matter of them not being bound to the Loom by virtue of being sufficiently 'big'. (And also to get away from the perception that being outside of fate was a strictly evil dude trick).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850221#post850221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Ox-Body looks really weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Ox-Body classically is an additional -0 health level.<br /> Hrm.<br /> <br /> Stamina 1-2: One -1 health level<br /> Stamina 3-4: One -0 health level<br /> Stamina 5: One -0 and one -2 health level.<br /> <br /> Better?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850221#post850221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial Artist should probably be completely free for Sids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeh, I feel like there still needs to be a slight gateway to show your study of a particular style. (I mean, correct me if I'm wrong, but you do have to buy the merit per style, yes?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850221#post850221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that take on Resplendent Destinies is a good idea. Letting Sidereals muck with ability dots like that basically means that they all have 5 (or occasionally 6) dots in every ability as long as they have motes to spend or time to prepare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeh. I look at as in the same vein of Social Personas- part of their purpose is to enable you to solve problems not suited to your natural skills.<br /> <br /> I also don't see having a 5 in something as being *that* big a deal- and not every Destiny is going to let you go to 6 in the relevant skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T17:16:20-07:00","id":850328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850286#post850286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes sense and is concise. Although it depends on what you want to do with the omens for higher Essence Charms. Are they the key to avoiding and preventing such powerful and devilishly subtle magic that only a true master of Lore could see them coming? As a challenge to high Lore players faced with a Sidereal opponent (only they can see the signs) or PC Sidereals faced with a the same high Lore opponent. In which case they should have pretty high difficulty. Or more the significant drawback and balance to some seriously high power Charms, where it makes sense that the Charm's power is such that even a person of quite low learning can feel it in the air, and in the water, when it is coming for them? This is as a drawback for Sidereal players to consider and to have to use their subterfuge and cunning if they want to conceal the omen. In which case decreasing difficulty with higher essence works well. I feel like the latter for sure is more your goal, but wanted to sound that one out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much more the later. Invoking their greatest powers bends the Heavens to the Sidereal's designs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T17:36:09-07:00","id":850336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850327#post850327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rakan Thulio sure the hell is outside of Fate. Saturn made her mark against him, and he went 'Fuck that shit', then tore his thread from the Loom with blasphemous power. Dude is out of fate as fuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blocking Saturn's mark should be a standard Essence 1 thing for every Celestial Exalt, as it is for Solars. And if he's a Sidereal, which he is, he's more inside Fate than anyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850327#post850327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Maidens and the Incarna- it's more a matter of them not being bound to the Loom by virtue of being sufficiently 'big'. (And also to get away from the perception that being outside of fate was a strictly evil dude trick).</div> </div> </div> </div>That strikes me as daft. Especially if you're trying to make being outside of Fate a lateral thing and not a strict benefit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850327#post850327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal Ox-Body classically is an additional -0 health level.<br /> Hrm.<br /> <br /> Stamina 1-2: One -1 health level<br /> Stamina 3-4: One -0 health level<br /> Stamina 5: One -0 and one -2 health level.<br /> <br /> Better?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it still seems pretty weak to me. I'd go with -0/-0,-2/-0,-0.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850327#post850327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eeh, I feel like there still needs to be a slight gateway to show your study of a particular style. (I mean, correct me if I'm wrong, but you do have to buy the merit per style, yes?)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're wrong. The merit is one time only. And you shouldn't change that; people waste enough xp buying the Ability multiple times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850327#post850327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eeh. I look at as in the same vein of Social Personas- part of their purpose is to enable you to solve problems not suited to your natural skills.<br /> <br /> I also don't see having a 5 in something as being *that* big a deal- and not every Destiny is going to let you go to 6 in the relevant skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abilities are a big part of what differentiates characters. If everyone is always 10m away from having whatever Ability they need, characters get same-y.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T04:57:35-07:00","id":850498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850336#post850336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blocking Saturn's mark should be a standard Essence 1 thing for every Celestial Exalt, as it is for Solars. And if he's a Sidereal, which he is, he's more inside Fate than anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Da book, pg 64</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:DINAlternate-Bold\"><b>Using forbidden martial </b><b>techniques, he tapped into a power feared even by the </b><b>Demon Princes, and marked himself as an enemy of </b><b>Heaven. When Saturn made her Sign against him, he turned </b><b>it aside with blasphemous power, and tore the thread of </b><b>his destiny from the Loom of Fate. For this, Thulio was cast </b><b>out of Heaven. Only then did Yu-Shan learn the scope of </b><b>his ambitions.</b></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>That is not a 'standard Essence 1 thing'. Thulio is seriously as outside of Fate as you get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850336#post850336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That strikes me as daft. Especially if you're trying to make being outside of Fate a lateral thing and not a strict benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting the Incarna outside of Fate is part of making it a lateral move- when only the Big Bads of the setting are outside of fate, it looks like a BBEG power up. Making it a quality of the Incarna as well helps emphasize that being outside of Fate doesn't make you *bad*, it marks you as metaphysically *big*.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850336#post850336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but it still seems pretty weak to me. I'd go with -0/-0,-2/-0,-0.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Ox-Body has always previously been an additional -0.<br /> The new Solar Ox-Body goes 'Stamina 1-2: A little worse than traditional. Stamina 3-4: Traditional. Stamina 5: A little better than traditional'.<br /> Why should the new Sidereal Ox-Body be so much better?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850336#post850336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're wrong. The merit is one time only. And you shouldn't change that; people waste enough xp buying the Ability multiple times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough! Then, yeah, every Sidereal should get the Merit for free.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850336#post850336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abilities are a big part of what differentiates characters. If everyone is always 10m away from having whatever Ability they need, characters get same-y.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Maybe there needs to be more restrictions on where the ability dots get shuffled- that way, it at least requires donning an appropriate Destiny, and encourages purchasing multiple of them.<br /> <br /> OTOH, I don't think that would address your fundamental concern, which I... just, don't share. Characters are differentiated by attributes, intimacies, and Charms as much or more than by their abilities in my experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:09:09-07:00","id":850559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850498#post850498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not a 'standard Essence 1 thing'. Thulio is seriously as outside of Fate as you get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Destiny Manifesting Method and a stunt. Seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850498#post850498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting the Incarna outside of Fate is part of making it a lateral move- when only the Big Bads of the setting are outside of fate, it looks like a BBEG power up. Making it a quality of the Incarna as well helps emphasize that being outside of Fate doesn't make you *bad*, it marks you as metaphysically *big*.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just makes it seem more like a power-up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850498#post850498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal Ox-Body has always previously been an additional -0.<br /> The new Solar Ox-Body goes 'Stamina 1-2: A little worse than traditional. Stamina 3-4: Traditional. Stamina 5: A little better than traditional'.<br /> Why should the new Sidereal Ox-Body be so much better?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it should be strictly worse than the Solar version. Wasn't in 2e, don't see why it should be now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850498#post850498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Maybe there needs to be more restrictions on where the ability dots get shuffled- that way, it at least requires donning an appropriate Destiny, and encourages purchasing multiple of them.<br /> <br /> OTOH, I don't think that would address your fundamental concern, which I... just, don't share. Characters are differentiated by attributes, intimacies, and Charms as much or more than by their abilities in my experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't believe me, go ahead and play with it. I'm confident it won't work out well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:44:54-07:00","id":850583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850559#post850559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it should be strictly worse than the Solar version. Wasn't in 2e, don't see why it should be now.</div> </div> </div> </div>... What? In 1e and 2e Sidereals, the Sidereal Ox-Body was fixed at an additional -0 health level.<br /> <br /> It was always strictly worse than the Solar Ox-Body (or any other Ox-Body, really), emphasizing Sidereals as glass ninjas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:58:53-07:00","id":850597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850583#post850583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... What? In 1e and 2e Sidereals, the Sidereal Ox-Body was fixed at an additional -0 health level.<br /> <br /> It was always strictly worse than the Solar Ox-Body (or any other Ox-Body, really), emphasizing Sidereals as glass ninjas.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not strictly worse. A single -0 HL was one of the options from the Solar Ox-Body, and there was no other way to gain -0 HLs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:02:40-07:00","id":850641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850597#post850597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not strictly worse. A single -0 HL was one of the options from the Solar Ox-Body, and there was no other way to gain -0 HLs.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, in that there wasn't an option. And further, again, the new Solar Ox-Body doesn't provide that as an option, but rather only the option with the most health levels.<br /> <br /> Assuming that the pattern of Stamina 1-2: a little worse than previous, Stamina 3-4: The previous value, Stamina 5: A little better than previous - I don't see how you can't put an additional -0 HL in the Stamina 3-4 section and pivot based on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T14:22:40-07:00","id":852013,"title":"","content":"Based on the volume of changes, I decided to create a new post rather than perform an edit in place.<br /> <br /> CHANGELOG:<br /> * In general, these changes are meant to emphasize the Mast more- which meant moving the soak-enhancing charms out. The Mast is stoic and strong, but it provides no protection- that is more the purview of the Shield, which is where such charms will be found.<br /> * In particular...<br /> *** Someone Else's Destiny will be moved to Athletics (The Rising Smoke, which governs murder. Nothing really explicitly covers poison that I could find)<br /> *** Optimistic Security Practice, Water and Fire Legion, and Storm's Eye Stance will all be moving to Presence (The Shield - Protection)<br /> * Broke the 'reshuffle ability points' element of Resplendent Destiny of the Mast into a repurchase, and limited the abilities it can fill in to limit the omni-competence problem.<br /> * There are several new charms. In part, this is because there are many more hooks, and Sidereals should have tools to interact with them. It is also to better represent the breadth of the constellation- The Mast governs Stoicism, Tools, Architecture, Manual Labor, Silence and Ignorance.<br /> <br /> Resplendent Destiny of the Mast<br /> Cost: - (10m); Mins: Resistance 1, Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> The Sidereal creates a new persona, a character of the Mast. The intimacies selected must be appropriate for an archtype of the Mast, relating to the appropriate associations.<br /> For example, the Resplendent Destiny may have a tie of admiration towards Ragara Yukio, a noted architect and geomancer; or perhaps a principle of disdain towards scholars and other individuals of book learning.<br /> <br /> An Essence 2+ repurchase of this charm allows you to more fully realize the persona. Redistribute all dots you have in Linguistics, Investigation, Socialize, Lore or Bureaucracy amongst Resistance, Ride, Sail, Survival, Thrown, Craft, Dodge, Athletics, and Brawl.<br /> You may raise Resistance to 6.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Ox-Body Technique<br /> Cost: -; Mins: Resistance 1, Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Stackable<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> As per the Solar Charm 'Ox-Body Technique', except:<br /> <br /> Stamina 1-2: An additional -1 health level<br /> Stamina 3-4: An additional -0 health level<br /> Stamina 5+: An additional -0 and -2 health level<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Forward Thinking Technique<br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Resistance 3, Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Until released<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> A laborer is nothing without their tools; by the virtue of the Mast, you are never so deprived. You may always call to hand any mundane tool you need for a task you are presently working on. The item vanishes once it is no longer being used for the job it was called for, and may never be either sold, traded or used in a fight.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Two Thousand Hands And Two<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Resistance 4, Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Stackable, Design<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Forward Thinking Technique<br /> <br /> The blessing of the Mast ensures that your labor is swift and easy- even the largest projects fall before you in short order. Each time you use this charm, you gain a Major Project slot for as long as you keep the motes committed. You may not purchase more Major Project slots than you have dots of Essence.<br /> If you work on the project exclusively in the destiny of the Mast, you may re-roll all 1s and 2s on your Craft rolls.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3, you may instead commit 15m to gain a Superior Project slot. Such a slot may only be used for large-scale mundane works, such as building a ship or a palace, and enable to Sidereal to work on the project alone- seemingly tirelessly accomplishing what should require teams of people. You may not purchase more than one such Superior Project slot at a time.<br /> Using this Charm makes the projects a matter of destiny; those interested in them may note the omens prophesying their successful completion.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> The Wisdom of Drudges<br /> Cost: -; Mins: Resistance 5, Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Two Thousand Hands and Two<br /> <br /> Hard work is it's own reward, and the dreamless sleep that accompanies a day's labor is sweeter than wine. You gain 1 silver point per 10 rolled on any Basic Project, 1 gold point per 10 rolled on any Major Project, and 3 gold points per 10 rolled on any Superior Project.<br /> If you work on the project exclusively in the destiny of the Mast, you may re-roll 10s as well, gaining successes and bonus points, until no 10s appear.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Scry the Hearthstone<br /> Cost: 3m, 1lhl; Mins: Resistance 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Forward Thinking Technique<br /> <br /> All architects belong to the Mast, and the blood and sweat of builders sanctify every structure to the stars. By giving an offering of blood, you may gain an intuitive understanding of the layout of a building- including any secret doors, hidden rooms, or mechanical traps.<br /> You do not learn anything magical about the building- if an illusion conceals a door, you may know the door is there, but still not be able to see it. Nor do you learn anything of the building's occupants.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3, you may also spend 1 willpower when activating Scry the Hearthstone; if you do, you also learn where all of the building's occupants are at that moment.<br /> <br /> Scry the Hearthstone may not be used on buildings raised by sorcery or the glamours of the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Strength of the Mast<br /> Cost: 1m / dot; Mins: Resistance 4, Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Resplendent Destiny of the Mast<br /> <br /> Under the blessing of the Mast, you can perform improbable feats of brute strength. For a single attack or feat of strength, you may temporarily increase your Strength score by 1 per mote of Essence. You may not more than double your natural Strength with this charm.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> A Place to Stand<br /> Cost: 3m / die; Mins: Resistance 5, Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Strength of the Mast<br /> <br /> Beyond improbable, you can now do the impossible- engaging in feats of strength that defy reason or explanation. For every three motes spent, set aside one die on a Feat of Strength roll; that die is automatically a 10. You may set aside no more than your Resistance in dice this way.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Ignorance is Bliss<br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Resistance 3, Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> The Mast knows nothing- neither of the wider world, nor of their own limits. For a moment, neither do you- all pain and fatigue fading into a fog of ignorance. You may ignore all penalties caused by pain, fatigue, poison, or any other purely internal affliction for one action.<br /> Additionally, you may forget yourself for a moment- concealing your true emotions beneath a mask of guileless ignorance. Add half your Resistance to your Guile or on any social action to convince someone of your simple-mindedness as non-charm successes.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Invisible at the Center<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Resistance 5, Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Design<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Ignorance is Blisss<br /> <br /> Laborers are everywhere, and yet they easily go unseen; one dullard drudge looking much like the next. You share in this unique invisibility; as long as you are performing hard manual labor with a group, you are invisible.<br /> Taking any overt actions or participating in activities other than manual labor ends this charm.<br /> Certain Charms may aid in detecting the Exalt. Roll the Sidereals\u2019s ([Stamina or Strength] + Stealth) against her opponent\u2019s relevant (Attribute + Ability) or Resolve, if the attacking Charm is based on the opponent\u2019s Integrity<br /> <br /> Each week past the first, destiny strains a little more at the deception. Omens begin to declare the presence of the Sidereal amongst the workers, and the difficulty to understand these omens drops by 1 per week. Weeks in which you wear the Destiny of the Mast do not count; Creation expects laborers to go unnoticed.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Unwavering Well-Being Meditation<br /> Cost: 1m / level; Mins: Resistance 5, Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Ignorance is Bliss<br /> <br /> Like the Mast, you bear punishment with stoic silence, drawing strength from the pain and victory seemingly from the jaws of defeat. When struck by a decisive blow, you may spend up to 1m per level of damage you take. You gain 1 initative per mote spent in this fashion. You may not spend more than your dots of Essence on this charm.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Heartless Maiden Trance<br /> Cost: 10m; Mins: Resistance 5, Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Unwavering Well-Being Meditation, Invisible at the Center<br /> <br /> You refine the lessons of ignorance, and learn to swallow your heart- becoming immune to all distresses and distractions of the body. While under the effects of Heartless Maiden Trance, you may ignore all penalties caused by pain, fatigue, poison, or any other purely internal affliction. You will not fall unconscious when your Incapacitated health level is taken; dying only when you have accrued (Stamina) additional levels of damage.<br /> Furthermore, poison, starvation and dehydration hang in abeyance until the charm ends, whereupon they all take effect at once.<br /> Finally, while under the Heartless Maiden Trance, you draw no nourishment from the world, and respire no essence outside of combat. Even in combat, the numbing chill of heartlessness leaves you respiring only 3 motes per turn.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Unswerving Juggernaut Principle<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Resistance 3, Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Destiny<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> You weave your arrival into the destiny of a location- as long as you do nothing but run towards that destination, you can continue to run towards that destination. While Unswerving Juggernaut Principle is active, you do not need to eat, drink or rest, and ignore damage or impairment from any natural environmental hazard.<br /> In order to activate Unswerving Juggernaut Principle, you must be able to physically reach your destination by running, although you can also ride or take other transportation to arrive sooner. You must always be moving closer to your destination, however, and cannot stop to involve yourself in festivals or fighting; doing so ends the effects of the charm.<br /> <br /> While active, omens and portents will herald the arrival of the Sidereal.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> One Direction Invocation<br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp; Mins: Resistance 5, Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Design<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charms: The Wisdom of Drudges, Scry the Hearthstone, A Place to Stand, Unswerving Juggernaut Principle, Heartless Maiden Trance<br /> <br /> You inscribe a prayer strip on one side with the scripture of the Eternal Maiden, and on the reverse, a pledge of your name to accomplish some goal. The strip bursts into golden flame, and your accomplishment is written into the Heavens for the wise to recognize.<br /> While under the effect of One Direction Invocation, you gain a Defining Principle to accomplish your stated goal; this Principle may also be called on an unlimited number of times in social influence. You also suffer a -3 situational penalty to all actions which do not directly facilitate achieving your goal.<br /> However, any non-aggravated damage you have suffered heals at a rate of one level of lethal or bashing per turn, while aggravated damage heals at a rate of 1 level per day.<br /> <br /> At any time, you may end this Charm; it will also end automatically if your goal becomes impossible. If the charm ends with your goal not having been accomplished, your name and identity are forfeit; you must requisition a new name from Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T10:20:03-07:00","id":853049,"title":"","content":"Very rough cut of Sidereal's Ride - this tree is causing me all manner of heartburn.<br /> <br /> Ride: The Messanger<br /> Trappings: The Messenger has a mount and rides on urgent business. She is daring and armed. She carries a package, from which she cannot be separated.<br /> Correlations: Duty, bravery, arrogance, journeys, communication, selflessness, news<br /> <br /> The Scripture of the Desirable Maiden<br /> Once, there was a maiden\u2026<br /> \u2026whom many men wanted for their own.<br /> She stepped as softly as starlight.<br /> She shone with glory.<br /> And one by one, they came to claim her.<br /> She fled by the quickest route she found.<br /> \u201cWhy do you run?\u201d the storm clouds said.<br /> She said, \u201cI cannot help who drives me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ordained Bridle of Mercury (Get a familiar)<br /> Spirit-Shape Companion (Promote a familiar to demi-godhood)<br /> Godly Companion (Promote a familiar to full godhood)<br /> Breaking the Wild Mortal (Get an Acquintance)<br /> Yellow Path (Fastest route)<br /> Glory Path (Increase speed, ignore natural obsticles)<br /> Riding the Dragon (Turn an acquintance into a motherfucking Dragon)<br /> <br /> Iron Heart, Iron Horse: Perfect bravery while carrying a message<br /> Blow Wind Style: Ignore fatigue<br /> Field Mouse Rider: Ride your familiar, no matter what it is<br /> <br /> Spirit-Shape Companion and Godly Companion are moved (probably to the Sorcerer [Occult])<br /> Breaking the Wild Mortal is moved to either the Pillar or the Lovers (although the name may change)<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> Resplendent Destiny of the Messenger: Create a persona. With a (Essence++) repurchase, you gain a divine Familiar as a mount, usable only while you wear the Destiny. (Equivalent to Familiar 3)<br /> <br /> Ordained Bridle of Mercury: Get a horse! (Or other appropriate mount). Basically, whistle up Shadowfax or giant eagle rescue. (Getting a flying mount should probably be an Essence ++ benefit)<br /> <br /> Iron Heart: Immune to fear. Your mount is also immune to fear.<br /> <br /> Yellow Path: You know the fastest route to some destination. With a repurchase, you know the fastest route to achieve some goal. Fastest is not necessarily safest.<br /> <br /> Glory Path: While traveling the Yellow Path, you speed increases to a thing of legend. If mounted, your mount can gallop over any terrain, even water, up sheer cliffs, or across thin air without difficulty. Immune to fatigue while traveling the Glory Path.<br /> <br /> ~: You know a traveller\u2019s current destination.<br /> <br /> ~: You can Defend Other without using your action. (Bonus) when you Defend Other your mount. At Essence ++, you can use ~ up to Ride times per turn.<br /> <br /> ~: For a short time, you can understand and be understood without linguistic barriers.<br /> <br /> ~: You can social influence someone to fulfil their duty as if using a Minor Intimacy.<br /> <br /> ~: (Bonus) to Disengage, Withdraw and any other test of speed. (Bonus++) if in the Destiny of the Messenger<br /> <br /> Ride the Dragon: Transform a mortal who has a major positive intimacy towards you into a Lesser Elemental Dragon. Said dragon will tirelessly carry you to anywhere in Creation within the next 25 hours, after which it fades away, leaving the broken husk of your former friend in it\u2019s wake.<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> Ideas I had and discarded:<br /> * Speak with the voice of god when conveying a message from Heaven; people may not like it, they may ignore it, but no one who hears you can deny the truth of your words. (Feels out of theme and too easy)<br /> * Enlist a mortal to bear a message for you (If a Sidereal wants to delegate, they should have to delegate directly)<br /> * Know the value of a piece of information (Feels more like a Secrets thing)<br /> * Able to gain audiences with people of rank (Again, too obvious and easy)<br /> * Know where you are needed ('Needed' is subjective- this feels like it's basically asking the GM for a plot cookie. Might keep it as a Journey's anima effect tho)<br /> <br /> Ideas that I like but can't find effects to capture:<br /> * Something about heralding something.<br /> * Something about traveling at the speed of rumor / bad news.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:18:03-07:00","id":853070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850559#post850559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Destiny Manifesting Method and a stunt. Seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>...that's not at all how this Charm works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=850583#post850583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was always strictly worse than the Solar Ox-Body (or any other Ox-Body, really), emphasizing Sidereals as glass ninjas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a valuable theme to retain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:20:23-07:00","id":853071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=853070#post853070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a valuable theme to retain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as the Sidereals are, even in the 3e core, called out as the seemingly weakest of the Celestial Exalted- yes, I think so.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:21:46-07:00","id":853072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=853071#post853071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seeing as the Sidereals are, even in the 3e core, called out as the seemingly weakest of the Celestial Exalted- yes, I think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, wait? What page was this on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:24:50-07:00","id":853075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=853072#post853072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What, wait? What page was this on?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pg 48, in the 'So you wanna play a Sidereal' section (Masters of Fate)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:26:55-07:00","id":853076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=853071#post853071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as the Sidereals are, even in the 3e core, called out as the seemingly weakest of the Celestial Exalted- yes, I think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leaving out the following phrase &quot;in raw displays of force,&quot; isn't exactly an honest paraphrasing of the sentiment the book expresses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:29:40-07:00","id":853079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=853076#post853076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaving out the following phrase &quot;in raw displays of force,&quot; isn't exactly an honest paraphrasing of the sentiment the book expresses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When it comes to Ox-Body Technique, a charm deeply involved in displaying power with regards to raw displays of force?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:31:43-07:00","id":853082,"title":"","content":"I would have Ox-Body be the same for all Celestial Exalts, because I hate Power Tiers. The only reason why I kind of accept it for Dragonblooded is because there are like ten thousand of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:39:34-07:00","id":853086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=853082#post853082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have Ox-Body be the same for all Celestial Exalts, because I hate Power Tiers. The only reason why I kind of accept it for Dragonblooded is because there are like ten thousand of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That line of reasoning runs towards homogenizing all the Exalts, which I rather disagree with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:43:57-07:00","id":853088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=853086#post853086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That line of reasoning runs towards homogenizing all the Exalts, which I rather disagree with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only a charm that gives a character health levels* and one of two charms that is shared among splats. Also, I think the Exalted Splats are differentiated by how their powers can be used to approach situations not how many health levels they have. A Sidereal's Dodge Charms are going to work differently than a Solar's or a Dragonblood's dodge charms. I don't think surviving longer in a fight would Homogenize all the Exalts.<br /> <br /> Though I think it is really cool you are working on converting Sidereals to Ex3. Always good to see different takes on it.<br /> <br /> *That I remember. I haven't read the Ex3 Resistance charms too closely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-25-2016, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T12:20:19-07:00","id":853108,"title":"","content":"Ox-Body isn't a display of anything. It's usually invisible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=853070#post853070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...that's not at all how this Charm works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it is.<br /> <br /> &quot;When struck with a reality-shaping or fate-weaving <br /> attack that would permanently alter her mind or body, the <br /> Solar\u2019s destiny manifests to override the changes. This <br /> Charm does not completely nullify deleterious effects...&quot;<br /> <br /> Saturn's mark is definitely a reality-shaping attack or fate-weaving attack that'll permanently alter you. Reducing the effect from &quot;you die&quot; to &quot;your thread of fate is torn, with the following effects...&quot; or saying &quot;you are dying, but you can fix the problem by going to the Loom and tearing out your thread&quot; would both be fair ways to run the Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T12:24:00-07:00","id":853111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=853079#post853079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When it comes to Ox-Body Technique, a charm deeply involved in displaying power with regards to raw displays of force?</div> </div> </div> </div>More health levels are involved with regards to raw displays of force? Man that's a huge stretch. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=853082#post853082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have Ox-Body be the same for all Celestial Exalts, because I hate Power Tiers. The only reason why I kind of accept it for Dragonblooded is because there are like ten thousand of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. It's a charm that has the same broad effect for all splats (more HP), I don't see much thematic value in Sidereals' being shittier. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=853108#post853108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure it is.<br /> <br /> &quot;When struck with a reality-shaping or fate-weaving <br /> attack that would permanently alter her mind or body, the <br /> Solar\u2019s destiny manifests to override the changes. This <br /> Charm does not completely nullify deleterious effects...&quot;<br /> <br /> Saturn's mark is definitely a reality-shaping attack or fate-weaving attack that'll permanently alter you. Reducing the effect from &quot;you die&quot; to &quot;your thread of fate is torn, with the following effects...&quot; or saying &quot;you are dying, but you can fix the problem by going to the Loom and tearing out your thread&quot; would both be fair ways to run the Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, somewhere between reading your post and looking up the Charm my brain reinterpreted you referencing &quot;Saturn's sign&quot; to &quot;all astrology effects&quot; as things the Charm could stop. S'pose you're right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 03-25-2016, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T13:15:20-07:00","id":853142,"title":"","content":"Note that &quot;Saturn making her sign against him&quot; can also be taken to mean &quot;he reached the natural end of his lifespan&quot; or similarly &quot;normal&quot; moment when one would die, such as from stabbing, which doesn't involve any shaping. Maybe he found a way to give himself an infinite lifespan, or to be invulnerable to damage.<br /> <br /> It's not out-of-theme for legends to be phrased ambiguously, and taking it to mean literally the least impressive thing possible is probably not the intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T13:30:02-07:00","id":853145,"title":"","content":"I don't think it being a standard effect for Celestials makes it less impressive. Actually, I think saying &quot;no matter who you are, you can't kill the Exalted without getting your hands dirty&quot; is pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> And in general, I think it's better if the mighty feats of the Elder Exalted are things that players can also do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T13:42:18-07:00","id":853151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/849962-if-i-were-writing-sidereals?p=853145#post853145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it being a standard effect for Celestials makes it less impressive. Actually, I think saying &quot;no matter who you are, you can't kill the Exalted without getting your hands dirty&quot; is pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> And in general, I think it's better if the mighty feats of the Elder Exalted are things that players can also do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh of course, i agree, but when writers trying to set up an NPC as a badass and that one of his more unique(-ish) feats is that he defied Fate itself, pointing out something like &quot;well, all charms are said to defy the loom so clearly he only used an excellency&quot; is <i>probably</i> not the intended interpretation.<br /> <br /> A unique (but PC-accessible) Martial Art or High-Essence Charm or, hell, even a Working to rewrite one's own rules of death, might be more along the intended lines. (In Thulio's case it's supposedly Martial Arts, iirc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 03-25-2016, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T17:51:35-07:00","id":854754,"title":"","content":"So, a couple of correlations that I've found I'm missing in the Sidereal constellations, which sort of surprised me- Trade (specifically trade routes, peddlers and merchants), and caravans / people travelling in groups.<br /> <br /> I suppose that both *could* fit under the Captain, but- am I just blind, or does some Constellation already cover these concepts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T04:19:24-07:00","id":854984,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think the Captain is a bad fit for these except in the case where they're led by an actual Captain-like figure.<br /> <br /> The Rising Smoke could handle many kinds of itinerant labor including peddlers:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the constellation of the young man, the journeyman, the corpse on its way to burial, the pubescent Dynast who has not yet Exalted, those up on charges or entangled by lawsuits and death by accident, heart attack, stroke and murder.<br /> <br /> Correlations: Quick and painless deaths, rest, stagnation, growth, new employment, fresh prospects, murder </div> </div> </div>The Messenger could work for some other merchants:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Messenger is the constellation of the courier, the valet, the aide, the diplomat, the young Terrestrial living in the household of her cousins, non-migratory birds including raptors and owls and of service to one\u2019s family.<br /> <br /> Trappings: The Messenger has a mount and rides on urgent business. She is daring and armed. She carries a package, from which she cannot be separated.<br /> <br /> Correlations: Duty, bravery, arrogance, journeys, communication, selflessness, news </div> </div> </div>For caravans / traveling in groups, I think there really isn't anything great, although depending on the character of the group any of the Serenity constellations might be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T06:45:59-07:00","id":855045,"title":"","content":"Itinerant labor seems to fall under the Mast, to me (the whole 'success through main strength and DOING HARDER' thing)- I'm more thinking the common fantasy trope of the traveling peddler or tinker (which- maybe that's kind of the Messanger, since they tend to be relatively solitary, skilled, proud, and often carry news as much as goods).<br /> <br /> As I've thought about it, I've also come to the conclusion that the Captain is appropriate for caravan like travel, since most caravans have a central leading figure. Ships at sea are the most obvious, but wagon caravans will have a leader deciding where to go and when to stop and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T07:31:21-07:00","id":855062,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sail: The Captain</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Scripture of the Maiden at Sea</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once, there was a maiden\u2026</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2026who set sail with a captain she did not know.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">She noticed the ship was crushing the waves and told the Captain to steer the ship higher so that it could be above them. \u201cBut not too high,\u201d she said. \u201cI\u2019d hate to crush the clouds.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The sea came over the side as a creature with teeth.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So, she set it on fire, until only the teeth were left. It wasn\u2019t expecting that to happen.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A face in the depths glared at the Captain. The maiden got angry.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">She broke the face and broke the depths and broke the sea, leaving only the white caps of the waves. \u201cWhy did you do that?\u201d asked the face.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cRarely is travel peaceful,\u201d the maiden said</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trappings: The Captain wears an emblem of rank and carries a token of authority such as a scepter or wand of office. He is fearless, and he shows no sign of fatigue. He is not kind, but he is always fair and concerned for the well-being of his followers.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correlations: Military command, fatherhood, tyranny, bureaucracy, discipline, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>people working together to travel</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">---------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resplendent Destiny of the Captain: You create an appropriate persona. With a repurchase, you may gain either Command 3 as an officer in a military organization in Creation, or Backing 3 within an organization in Creation. When you are not bearing this destiny, your troops or department disperse amongst the remainder of the army or bureaucracy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Knowing Pater: You speak with the voice of a character's parents, able to leverage any intimacies they have towards their family.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stern Master's Rebuke: You radiate terror and command respect. (Weaker but not obvious Terrifying Apparition of Glory)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Will of the Whip: You either bless a leader to have troops fight better together, or curse them to fight worse; improving Average troops to Elite or reducing them to Poor. (Bonus) when used for the crew of a ship or caravan.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Iron Drill Exercise: Tiger Warrior Training Technique. (I mean, not exactly, but pretty much)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attitude of Tyrants: As long as you act like it, people treat you like you are in charge. If you are seen hesitating or taking orders, the effect is broken.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shouting at the Wind: You demand that the weather calm down, and it does in your immediate vicinity- storms may rage around you, but you have calm seas and fair winds.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Salt Into Ash Sleight: You order a spirit of water to depart. With a repurchase, you can order any spirit impeding a group\u2019s journey to depart.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mirror Shattering Method: You can lead a group to a distant location over several days of magical travel (farther/faster when sailing) (replaces Five Ordeals Odyssey as the capstone)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>What happened to Five Ordeals Odyssey?</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Five Ordeals Odyssey was a bit of an odd duck, even by Sidereal Charm standards. Rather than directly help you overcome a problem, it rewards you for having overcome- by both finishing the problem off and temporarily raising your Essence. It may make a return as a Sorcery spell, but it does not feel like a \u2018Charm\u2019 as a \u2018Extension of your ability to work within an area\u2019.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:41:34-07:00","id":856142,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Survival: The Ship's Wheel</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scripture of the Maiden Entombed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once there was a maiden... </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">who lived in a tomb and the tomb was made in her image.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Because she lived in a tomb, she became like the Dead. She slept and dreamed.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And sometimes she woke and walked within the confines of her tomb.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Why do you move; &quot; her own ghost asked. &quot;Why walk at all?&quot;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;I'm not trapped while yet I run&quot; said she.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trappings: The steersman at the wheel is sleepless and unwashed. He wears a long cape or jacket and wristlets or a belt of rope. The steersman has a determined demeanor and is unspeaking, for none can share the burden of his post.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correlations: Underdogs, cult beliefs, Solars, obsessive love, martyrdom, burdensome debt, wild animals as a group</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">----</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resplendent Destiny of the Ship\u2019s Wheel: Create a persona. With a repurchase, you gain the ability to speak with wild (not domesticated) animals while wearing this destiny.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dawn of a new Day: You know when and where in Creation the most recent Solar Exaltation occurred. Dawn of a new Day cannot be used more than once per day, and cannot be used during Calibration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Finger on the Scale: You may spend up to (Essence) motes to add dice in any contested roll, for yourself or another, up to equaling the character with the greatest dice pool before Excellencies are used. Dice added in this way do count against dice caps.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A New Apocalypse: Provide a revelation that can change a cult\u2019s beliefs</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Marshaling Infinite Strength: You enflame a positive tie into an obsession- unless the obsession is fulfilled. Target gains bonuses while following this obsession, penalties when resisting it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sky Spirit Demand: Impose a task on a spirit of air (or, at greater difficulty any other spirit of creation\u2019s wilds)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Poetic Sacrifice Utilization: When someone in a group you travel with dies, you can take some of their escaping purpose and use it to help everyone else. The death must come from privation, disease or exposure- in other words, it must have been hard and lingering, not from combat or a knife in the night- but it *can* be arranged by the Sidereal that the target suffers from the sickness or privation. For the next (Survival) days, the unit needs neither food nor water, inspired by the example of their fallen comrade. If it was the leader of the unit that died, this instead works for the next (Survival) weeks. If the member that died was Exalted, regardless of if they were the leader, it worked for the next (Survival) months. You may use this Charm at the moment of your own death, in which case it\u2019s effects endure until it ends. This blessing ends when the unit completes its current journey.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Possess the Land: You inscribe a prayer strip with the scripture of the Maiden Entombed, and cast it into the sky. It unfurls, extending for miles, marking the boundaries of your land. You take possession of a stretch of wilderness with a radius equal to your Essence. You can dictate the weather, make travel and survival in the area easy or difficult, add your Survival to any Awareness rolls made in the area, and shift around the geography and characteristics of the region.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T14:23:43-07:00","id":856716,"title":"","content":"Thrown: The Gull<br /> <br /> The Scripture of the Maiden and Shadow<br /> <br /> Once, there was a maiden\u2026<br /> \u2026whose shadow fled from her. She chased it over fire and stone.<br /> She chased her shadow to a monster\u2019s mouth. Her shadow went right in. It didn\u2019t know how to stop.<br /> The maiden caught her shadow in a deep cave full of ghosts. Her shadow turned into a ball of thorns that wrapped around her. When the ghosts pricked their fingers on the thorns, they came to life. This didn\u2019t make anyone very happy.<br /> The maiden made a ladder from the ghosts\u2019 bones, but it only pointed downward. \u201cWhy go on?\u201d her shadow asked.<br /> \u201cI can\u2019t quit now,\u201d said she.<br /> <br /> Trappings: The Gull carries a staff and wears a traveler\u2019s cape. He is dirty and hungry but also happy.<br /> Correlations: Wandering, wind, irresponsibility, rakish charisma, unexamined life, smugglers<br /> <br /> Resplendent Destiny of the Gull: Create a persona. With a repurchase, when you get a good night's sleep after accomplishing nothing but enjoying yourself and travelling at an easy pace the day before, you gain two willpower instead of one.<br /> <br /> Life Gets Worse: If an attack supplemented with Life Gets Worse misses, you may make an immediate Distract gambit. Life Gets Worse may explicitly be used to supplement any Thrown, Archery, Brawl, Melee, or Martial Arts attack; when used to enhance a Thrown attack, it costs (discount)<br /> <br /> Casting Away Cares: You can briefly divest yourself of your concerns, giving them to your enemies instead. You form a light throwing weapon from one of your Intimacies. If used to make a withering attack, reduce the TN of the attack by 1 for a Minor Intimacy, 2 for a Major Intimacy and 3 for a Defining Intimacy. If used to make a decisive attack which deals at least 2 levels of damage, your opponent must either pay 1/2/3 Willpower, or gain the Intimacy. Once thrown away, the intimacy is lost for (duration) and cannot be used again, either for Casting Away Cares or for resisting social influence.<br /> <br /> Knives Full of Wind: Supplement a thrown attack; regardless of the success of the attack, 1s subtract successes of any Rush action they take towards you for the next three turns. If the attack hits, 1s and 2s substract successes.<br /> <br /> Wandering Weapon Method: Supplement a decisive attack; you do not lose any initiative for the missed attack. In each subsequent turn, if you continue making decisive attacks against the same target enhanced by Wandering Weapon Method, increase the raw damage by 1 per attack, as the previously errant weapons come flying back.<br /> <br /> Honest Face Smile: When you attack someone who has a positive tie towards you, Observer-Deceiving Attack. Honest Face Smile may supplement any attack made with light thrown or light melee weapons.<br /> <br /> Pain Amplification Strategy: When you make a decisive thrown attack against someone who is in Initiative Crash, your damage TN is reduced by 1 for each turn they have been Crashed.<br /> <br /> Life of the Grasshopper: In even the most desolate of landscapes, you can find ample food and drink to suffice for yourself and (Essence) friends. <br /> <br /> Ties That Bind: When someone applies their Resolve against an instill action to join you travelling, you may make a reflexive read intentions action to know what, if any, intimacy they used.<br /> <br /> Unrelenting Torment Technique: Stick a prayer strip on your target with a brawl, martial arts or thrown decisive gambit that does no damage (difficulty 2). <br /> Until the end of the scene, or until you remove it, any attack which would deal you damage instead presents<br /> you with a choice:<br /> * That damage can be shunted onto someone that you feel an obligation or debt.<br /> towards, or<br /> * You can take twice the damage.<br /> <br /> You may voluntarily place the prayer strip on yourself.<br /> Unrelenting Torment Technique has no effect upon someone who genuinely feels no obligations towards anyone else; such shiftless wanders intersect with no other weave for Fate to send the damage towards, and the prayer strip simply slides off.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:39:27-07:00","id":857788,"title":"","content":"So, I've consolidated notes and charms into a single Google doc, along with thoughts on Caste abilities, character creation and Anima effects.<br /> <br /> BAM<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1T4FTsSprLYd8KWXgE5Rr1x7C9_B6Ln5cnGN8HF7a3Vk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1T4FTsSprLYd8KWXgE5Rr1x7C9_B6Ln5cnGN8HF7a3Vk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1T4FTsSprLYd8KWXgE5Rr1x7C9_B6Ln5cnGN8HF7a3Vk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1T4FTsSprLYd8KWXgE5Rr1x7C9_B6Ln5cnGN8HF7a3Vk/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T19:59:27-07:00","id":858697,"title":"","content":"Passes Craft and Dodge done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}